hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17630","Hushaym narrated to us: 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr informed us, from Iyad ibn Laqit, who said: Abu Rimthah al-Tamimi informed me, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of mine. He said: Is this your son? I said: Yes, I testify to it. He said: He shall not bear wrong on your behalf, nor shall you bear wrong on his behalf. He said: And I saw white hair dyed red."
"17631","Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us: 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar narrated to me, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my father, and he saw what was on his back. He said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not treat it for you, for I am a physician? He said: You are a companion, and Allah is the Physician. He said: Who is this with you? I said: My son. He said: Bear witness to him. He said: Indeed he shall not bear wrong against you, nor shall you bear wrong against him. The name of Abu Rimthah is Rifa'ah ibn Yathribi."
"17632","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Laqit al-Sadusi, from Abu Rimthah al-Tamimi, who said: I went out with my father until I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I saw on his head traces of henna, and on his shoulder like an apple. My father said: I am a physician, shall I not lance it for you? He said: Its Creator has made it wholesome. He said: And he said to my father: Is this your son? He said: Yes. He said: Indeed he shall not bear wrong on your behalf, nor shall you bear wrong on his behalf."
"17633","'Abd Allah narrated to us: Waki' narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Salih, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah al-Tamimi, who said: I was with my father, and we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah wearing two green cloaks."
"17634","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Mas'udi informed us, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was preaching and saying: The upper giving hand: your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the nearest, then the nearest. He said: A group from Banu Tha'labah ibn Yarbu' entered, and a man from the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, these Yarbu'i men are those who killed so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed no soul shall bear the wrong of another, twice."
"17635","'Abd Allah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar, he is Ibn al-Rayyan, narrated to us: Qays ibn al-Rabi' al-Asadi narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, who said: I set out with my father, and I was a boy, and we came to a man at midday sitting in the shade of a house wearing two green cloaks, his hair was wafrah, and on his head traces of henna. He said: My father said to me: Do you know who this is? I said: No. He said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned him."
"17636","'Abd Allah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us: Abu Sufyan al-Himyari, Sa'id ibn Yahya, narrated to us, who said: al-Dahhak ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dye with henna and katam, and his hair would reach his shoulders or his upper arms."
"17637","'Abd Allah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-'Ala', Abu Kurayb al-Hamdani, narrated to us: Ibn Idris narrated to us, who said: I heard Ibn Abjar, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah al-Tamimi, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my father, and he had locks with traces of henna on them, and he mentioned him."
"17638","'Abd Allah narrated to us: al-'Abbas al-Duri narrated to us: 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Iyad ibn Laqit, who said: Abu Rimthah narrated to me that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of his. He said: Is this your son? He said: Yes. He said: Indeed he shall not bear wrong on your behalf, nor shall you bear wrong on his behalf."
"17639","Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Azraq narrated to us: Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated to us: al-Dahhak ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dye with henna and katam, and his hair would reach his shoulders or his upper arms, Abu Sufyan doubted. Mu'adh repeated it."
